    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="1109" n="1009" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg1009"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.62M31/84</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Wellington</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bucklin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 40</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wellington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-12-04">December 4,
                        1934</date>.<lb/>[Received January 2, 1935.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s Instruction of October 18, 1934, File No. 611.62M31/82, in which
                    additional information is requested regarding the discrimination against
                    American commerce in Western Samoa.</p>
                <p>In reply to the Department’s questions, it is informed that the preference to
                    British goods accorded by the Samoan Customs applies equally to goods from all
                    portions of the British Empire. Also the Ottawa Agreements have not in any way
                    affected the Samoan tariff, as this latter has not been altered subsequent to
                    the Ottawa Conference, and the rates now in force, both preferential and
                    general, were those applicable before the Agreements negotiated at Ottawa came
                    into effect.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. A. Bucklin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
